# StudySync backend production environment
# Copied to C:\ProgramData\StudySync\app\api\.env during installation.

# --- Authentication ---
# Staff key that every request must send in the X-API-Key header.
# Generated fresh on each install (min. 32 chars, random).
# STAFF ENTER THIS ONCE on each browser in Settings → API Key.
STUDYSYNC_API_KEY=CHANGE_ME

# --- Database ---
# Keep the database outside the app folder so updates never touch data.
STUDYSYNC_DB_PATH=C:\ProgramData\StudySync\data\library.db

# --- CORS (optional extra origins) ---
# When served through Caddy everything is same-origin, so nothing is needed.
# Only add entries if you intentionally expose a second frontend elsewhere.
# STUDYSYNC_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=https://app.example.com

# --- ZKTeco biometric device (optional — leave commented to disable) ---
# ZK_DEVICE_IP=192.168.1.201
# ZK_DEVICE_PORT=4370
# ZK_COMM_KEY=0

# --- ZKTeco integration mode ---
# "pyzk" (default) | "none". "pyzk" mounts the PyZK poll/live/reconcile
# device integration (needs ZK_DEVICE_IP set above). "none" disables the
# device integration entirely. The legacy values "both"/"adms" are accepted
# and both mean "pyzk" now that the old ADMS push transport is removed.
# ZK_INTEGRATION=pyzk

# --- Attendance punch tuning ---
# Double-tap guard: a swipe within this many minutes of the student's last
# swipe on the same day is ignored. 0 disables it. (Default: 1)
# ZK_PUNCH_DEBOUNCE_MINUTES=1

# --- Device ATTLOG buffer management ---
# The MB360 keeps every punch in its on-device buffer until cleared. When the
# buffer fills past ZK_BUFFER_CLEAR_PERCENT (default 95%), the reconcile pass
# archives the whole buffer into a dated database
# (device_punches_YYYY-MM-DD.db) under ZK_BUFFER_ARCHIVE_DIR, then clears the
# device. Clearing only ever runs after every pulled record is verified to
# have a durable DB write, so no punch can be lost. The archived raw records
# stay on disk indefinitely for audit/re-import; the main library.db ledger
# is pruned aggressively.
# ZK_BUFFER_CLEAR_PERCENT=95
# ZK_BUFFER_ALERT_PERCENT=80
# ZK_BUFFER_AUTO_CLEAR=1            # 0 = keep StudySync a pure reader
# ZK_BUFFER_ARCHIVE_DIR=C:\ProgramData\StudySync\data\device_punches
# ZK_LEDGER_RETENTION_DAYS=30       # main-DB ledger safety window when buffer is empty

# --- Google Sheets cloud sync (optional — leave unset to disable) ---
# POST /api/sync pushes every module to its own worksheet (tab). The sheet
# must be shared with the service-account email (Editor access).
# GOOGLE_SPREADSHEET_ID=<the Google Sheet's long ID>
# GOOGLE_CREDS_FILE=<path to the service-account JSON key> (default: credentials.json)
# STUDYSYNC_SHEETS_MAX_CELLS_PER_REQUEST=<max cells per API write> (default: 100000)

# --- Google Drive backup mirror (optional — leave unset to disable) ---
# Every night backup.exe mirrors the local backup zips to a Google Drive
# folder and prunes remote copies older than the retention window. Create a
# folder in Drive and share it with the service-account email (Editor). The
# same GOOGLE_CREDS_FILE is reused.
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=<the Drive folder's ID (last segment of its URL)>
# STUDYSYNC_BACKUP_RETENTION_DAYS=30
